## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical crypto for multi-tenant KCNA: encryption at rest, per-tenant keys, rotation, and in-flight re-encryption.

## Key Concepts

- Envelope encryption
- Per-tenant DEKs
- KMS master key
- Rotation workflow
- Least privilege and auditing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-encryption flow for a tenant payload
function encryptPayload(tenantId, payload, dekStore, kms) {
  const dek = dekStore.getDEK(tenantId);
  const wrapped = kms.wrapKey(dek);
  const iv = crypto.randomBytes(12);
  const cipher = crypto.createCipheriv('aes-256-gcm', dek, iv);
  // ... encryption steps
  return { ciphertext, dekWrapped: wrapped };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you scale DEK storage and rotation across thousands of tenants?
- What if rotation fails during processing; how ensure atomicity and replay safety?

Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical deletion workflows in multi-tenant KCNA, balancing legal rights, data minimization, and system integrity. It requires concrete mappings, key management, tombstone strategies, and test plans that prove irreversibility while keeping performance acceptable.

Key Concepts

- Tenant-scoped data maps and identifiers
- Per-tenant key rotation and re-encryption
- Tombstones, garbage collection, and index scrubbing
- Auditing, proofs, and compliance testing
- Backups, restores, and consistency guarantees

Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation skeleton
function eraseTenantData(tenantId) {
  revokeAccess(tenantId);
  rotateKeys(tenantId);
  scrubIngest(tenantId);
  scrubEnrichment(tenantId);
  scrubAnalytics(tenantId);
  publishTombstones(tenantId);
}
```

Follow-up Questions

- How would you test for complete deletion in a live cluster?
- How do backups interact with the deletion policy?

## Why This Is Asked
Regulated multi-tenant data requires per-tenant privacy controls with verifiable audit trails and deterministic replay.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-scoped redaction
- Deterministic replay via sequence numbers
- Cryptographic receipts and audit roots
- Per-tenant policy evaluation
- Latency implications and backpressure handling

## Code Example
```javascript
function redact(record, policy){
  const out = {...record};
  if(policy.redactEmail) out.email = 'REDACTED';
  if(policy.redactIp) out.ip = 'REDACTED';
  if(policy.redactPhone) out.phone = 'REDACTED';
  // tokenization could be added here
  return out;
}
```

